  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q8",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Write $\\dfrac{2^n\\times8^n}{2^{2n}\\times16}$ in the form $2^{an+b}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2^{2n-4}$\n\nExpress every factor as a power of 2, then combine the indices.",
      "worked": "Using $8=2^3$ and $16=2^4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2^n\\times8^n}{2^{2n}\\times16}&=\\frac{2^n\\times(2^3)^n}{2^{2n}\\times2^4}\\\\\\frac{2^n\\times8^n}{2^{2n}\\times16}&=\\frac{2^{n+3n}}{2^{2n+4}}\\\\\\frac{2^n\\times8^n}{2^{2n}\\times16}&=2^{4n-(2n+4)}\\\\\\frac{2^n\\times8^n}{2^{2n}\\times16}&=2^{2n-4}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
